rail.prompt:
You are a code reviewer tasked with identifying "Feature Envy" technical debts in the provided code snippets. Please review the code snippet and identify any instances of Feature Envy technical debt.
Below, you will find a definition of "Feature Envy" technical debt.
###################################################### Technical Debt: Feature Envy - It is related to methods that use operations from external classes more often than their own operations. It occurs when a method in a class is overly reliant on the data or behavior of another class, often making extensive use of that external class's properties or methods. This smell indicates that the method may be more concerned with the responsibilities of the external class than its own, leading to poor encapsulation and reduced cohesion. Feature Envy makes the code less intuitive, harder to maintain, and can increase the likelihood of bugs because the method's true "home" is misplaced. To address this, the code is refactored by moving the method to the class it is most envious of, thereby promoting better object-oriented design and ensuring clearer responsibility distribution.
###################################################### Please analyze the following code snippets and report any instances of feature envy present in the code snippet.
###################################################### ${code_changes}
${output_schema}
${gr.json_suffix_prompt}
